		"description": "Complete API collection for the Sign Language Translation Backend.\n\n---\n\n## 🚀 Deployment\n\n**Backend (Railway):** https://newproject-production-396a.up.railway.app\n\n**AI Service (Local):** http://127.0.0.1:5000 (run locally)\n\n**AI Service (Railway):** https://ai-service-production-xxx.up.railway.app (replace with your generated Railway domain)\n\n---\n\n## 📌 Variables\n\n| Variable | Local Value | Railway Value |\n|---|---|---|\n| `baseUrl` | http://localhost:3000/api | https://newproject-production-396a.up.railway.app/api |\n| `aiBaseUrl` | http://127.0.0.1:5000 | https://your-ai-service-domain.up.railway.app |\n| `authToken` | Auto-filled after Login | Auto-filled after Login |\n\n---\n\n## 📋 Steps\n1. Run **Register** to create account\n2. Run **Login** → Token saved automatically ✅\n3. Use any protected endpoint (Token added automatically)\n4. Test AI directly from **🤖 AI Service (Direct)** folder\n\n💡 *Tip: To switch between Local and Railway, just change the values of `baseUrl` and `aiBaseUrl` in the Collection Variables tab in Postman.*",
